Package: newsindex
Title: News-Based Economic Policy Uncertainty (EPU) Indices
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Shakir Adeyemi", "Tewogbade", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "113283849+chaqBD@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Builds news-based Economic Policy Uncertainty (EPU) indices
    from newspaper archives, implementing the method behind the CAPE
    Africa EPU Index (Baker, Bloom and Davis 2016, adapted for
    multilingual African press). Provides Unicode-aware multilingual
    term matching, country keyword dictionary loading and validation,
    article deduplication, newspaper-month counting against a frozen
    baseline, and GDP-PPP-weighted regional and Africa aggregation.
    This is the R counterpart of the Python 'newsindex' package
    (<https://github.com/CAPE-ERC/newsindex-library>); see that
    project's README for the full method.
